{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>Weight for weight.</b> In chapter קמא of Ketubot they said that one should not place a weight in its weight, and Rashi explained: not to do as the weighers do — when they weigh one thing and wish to weigh another like it, they take the object they weighed off the scales and then weigh against that weighed object the thing they wish to weigh. And there are those who explained: one should not place the weight on a weight in the manner done with the marc balance in Old French, which is made of many weights nested one inside the other, small inside large — and one should not do thus. This I did not understand — why one should not do so."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "The Old French term 'מאר\"ק' is transliterated as 'marc'; the phrase 'בלע\"ז' (la'az = in the vernacular) indicates the Old French gloss that followed in the original."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:04:24.873145092Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}